A9 — CAUSED BY THIS CHANGE, DELIBERATELY NOT BOUGHT GREEN

  A9 requires all three predicates RED at the pinned baseline. 1 came back GREEN: P1.
  A predicate that is green at the baseline cannot fail and is therefore not a gate
  (spec.md §7 item 4). Fix the predicate; do not proceed to solicit a reply.

A9 re-derives the "three reds" from a live run of HEAD, so it can only ever pass while
all three defects are unfixed. P1's defect is now fixed and P1 reports CLOSED, with the
positive control completing a real channel — so A9 is red BECAUSE the fix landed, and its
message reads as an accusation against the predicate when the predicate is fine.

Nothing here was softened to clear it. Re-pinning T25's baseline record (read the recorded
baseline reds from evidence rather than from a re-run of HEAD) is a governance decision
about T25's handshake, not a security control, and it is left to the integrator.

The baseline red A9 exists to preserve IS recorded, verbatim, in
02-P1-baseline-OPEN-before-the-fix.log:
  case absent-identity: the client COMPLETED the channel (expectedDoorStatic pinned=false)
  the client PROCEEDED in 1 of 2 case(s): absent-identity — a channel reached transport
  mode with no door identity checked. P1 OPEN

